      "explanation": "The same llama.cpp source and the same quant target produce different bytes because quantize_row_q4_0_ref computes `x*id + c`: with -ffp-contract=fast (GCC's default, the dgxspark build) that is one FMA, without it (Apple clang's default) it is `fmul` + `fadd`, and the two pick a different quant at an exact rounding boundary. Measured 2026-10-07 on dgxspark one variable at a time: HEAD 050dde50c with -O3 -DNDEBUG reproduces the dgxspark reference, and the same build with -ffp-contract=off gives ea94611e... minfer reproduces the -ffp-contract=fast build; the F6 parity gate detects which build a reference came from and names it (issue #334, PR #340). The Mac's full digests for these 11 files were not captured, only their 8-hex prefixes.",
      "references": [
        "docs/GGUF-TOOLING.md 4.2",
        "https://github.com/yusiwen/minfer/issues/334"
      ]
    }
